@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
top to bottom direction
title SysML IBD - context BLK-01 SmartTrafficLightSystem
actor TrafficDataSource as Source
frame "BLK-01 SmartTrafficLightSystem" {
 component "sensor : VehicleDetection\nBLK-02 [1]" as Sensor <<part>> {
  port "P01" as P01
  port "P02" as P02
 }
 component "analysis : DensityAnalysis\nBLK-03 [1]" as Analysis <<part>> {
  port "P03" as P03
  port "P04" as P04
 }
 component "controller : TrafficController\nBLK-04 [1]" as Controller <<part>> {
  port "P05" as P05
  port "P06" as P06
  port "P07" as P07
  port "P08" as P08
 }
 component "signals : SignalController\nBLK-05 [1]" as Signals <<part>> {
  port "P09" as P09
  port "P10" as P10
  port "P11" as P11
 }
 component "lights : TrafficLights[4]\nBLK-06" as Lights <<part>> {
  port "P12" as P12
 }
}
Source --> Sensor : provided counts\n(environment boundary input)
P01 --> P03 : C01 / CountsFrame
P04 --> P05 : C02 / DensityFrame
P02 --> P06 : C03 / fault, streak
P07 --> P09 : C04 / PhaseCommand
P10 --> P08 : C05 / BoundaryEvent
P11 --> P12 : C06 / LampVector
legend bottom
<<part>> is a renderer annotation for a SysML part property.
Port IDs P01-P12: typed proxy ports; types/endpoints in model dictionary.
Each directed connector line combines an assembly connector with an item flow;
arrow indicates item direction, not a satisfy dependency.
P12 is a bundled presentation of four conjugated port instances;
LampVector has exactly one entry per approach (fan-out by approach).
endlegend
@enduml
